    "title": "Nim Game Winner",
    "category": "Mathematics - Game Theory",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "problemStatement": "There is a single pile containing N stones. Two players take turns removing 1, 2, or 3 stones. The player who removes the last stone wins. Determine whether the first player has a winning strategy assuming both players play optimally.",
